Package: llmmetric
Title: Psychometric Validation and Inference for LLM-Coded Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
      given = "Marcus",
      family = "Harris",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com"
    )
Description: Treats large language models (LLMs) as fallible measurement
    instruments for research data. Orchestrates reproducible multi-facet
    coding designs with response caching, strict JSON schema validation, and
    pluggable API or deterministic mock backends; estimates Generalizability
    Theory variance components, reliability, D-study projections, calibration
    against human gold standards, temporal drift, and Differential Prompt
    Functioning (DPF); and implements Prediction-Powered Inference (PPI,
    PPI++, and clustered or multilevel extensions) for statistically valid
    downstream estimation and inference.
